            "pages": {
              "end": 13,
              "start": 13
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The majority held that the law permits suits against individuals in any jurisdiction where they can be found."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "5149e9957088896777c37e9b85b7b4f13b1039e3b1ca526cc9a4fff773c15bbc",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-5149e9957088-0002-0006"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 26,
              "start": 26
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Pennsylvania Supreme Court judgment was vacated and the case was remanded."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "5149e9957088896777c37e9b85b7b4f13b1039e3b1ca526cc9a4fff773c15bbc",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-5149e9957088-0005-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 53,
              "start": 53
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Barrett dissented, arguing that the plurality could not locate a historical case supporting its theory."
      }
    ],
