              "end": 6,
              "start": 6
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Robert Mallory, a former Norfolk Southern freight\u2011car mechanic, sued Norfolk Southern in Pennsylvania alleging exposure to carcinogens while working on freight\u2011car interiors."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Norfolk Southern",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "5149e9957088896777c37e9b85b7b4f13b1039e3b1ca526cc9a4fff773c15bbc",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-5149e9957088-0000-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 6,
              "start": 6
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Norfolk Southern argued that the Due Process Clause gives it a rule shielding it from suits in Pennsylvania."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "5149e9957088896777c37e9b85b7b4f13b1039e3b1ca526cc9a4fff773c15bbc",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-5149e9957088-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 13,
              "start": 13
            }
          },
          {
            "document_hash": "5149e9957088896777c37e9b85b7b4f13b1039e3b1ca526cc9a4fff773c15bbc",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-5149e9957088-0002-0006"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 26,
              "start": 26
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Court held that the law permits suits against individuals in any jurisdiction where they can be found, vacated the Pennsylvania Supreme Court judgment, and remanded the case."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "5149e9957088896777c37e9b85b7b4f13b1039e3b1ca526cc9a4fff773c15bbc",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-5149e9957088-0005-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 53,
              "start": 53
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Barrett dissented, stating that the plurality could not identify a single historical case supporting its theory."
      }
    ],
